Kitty ix86 Operating system
******************************
Do not build this code! Memory management is not done yet, so you'll face implicit function errors. Instead, wait for a new release.
The author is pretty sensitive, you'll make me cry of joy if you contribute >_<
^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
NEWS:-
KittyOS will soon be x86_64 aka amd64 and not ix86! It also needs UEFI, specifically UEFI GOP. This release will release soon, but its currently in an harsh stage of development. The ix86 version will still be there, but dont expect a Desktop or new commands. We're also building ViX (Vastly Improved X), still only for UEFI.
******************************
Imagine someone so unemployeed he made an entire,
non Linux-based operating system for his cat
hehehhehe >:]
-----------------------------
KittyOS needs an ix86 processor (compiled
with i686-elf-gcc). HOWEVER,
x86_64 (or amd64) is still supported via
instruction retrocompatibility!!
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
KittyOS needs to be compiled on arch-based
systems as Arch, CachyOS, Manjaro, etc. It includes a nice installer called devmkiso.
ALWAYS use devmkiso to build instead of manual
compilation. You find the steps for the manual
compilation in the devmkiso script (as it is
a normal Bourne Again SHell script >:D)
devmkiso requires the following packages:
GRand Unified BootLoader (you don't need to install GRUB as your bootloader, you just need the package)
i686-elf-gcc located in ~/opt/cross/* (you
can either compile it yourself
our check out lordmiiko's repo
to grab a precompiled one)
